  "reasoning": [
    "The36 copies are explicit consumer Copy→GGML DUP materializations immediately after native state reorder, not copies performed by StateHead publication or an accidental extra Graph crossing.",
    "Dropping Copy and borrowing an Invocation temporary would lose stable independently retained storage when that Invocation/workspace is reused.",
    "Publishing an owned2MiB parent plus readonly1MiB subview could be semantically correct, but requires changing caller output ports/bindings/pool sizing and declared cache budget. It is not a cost-free dedup within the present contract.",
    "The present copies deliberately preserve independently reclaimable candidate allocations and old readers. Keep the default for this bounded source review; do not extend K1 fusion or add a new split-lease abstraction for this candidate."
  ],
